      "title": "Nigeria confirms Ebola case as outbreak spreads into western Africa",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/21/nigeria-first-ebola-case-africa-outbreak-latest",
      "description": "<p>Case in Africa’s most populous country was detected in a woman who had travelled from Uganda</p><p>Nigeria has confirmed an Ebola case in its capital, Abuja, after a woman who arrived from Uganda tested positive for the virus, the health ministry said.</p><p>The woman began showing symptoms on 7 October and was admitted to a hospital in Abuja four days later, where she was later diagnosed with Ebola. It is unclear when she arrived in Nigeria, Africa’s most populous country.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/21/nigeria-first-ebola-case-africa-outbreak-latest\">Continue reading...</a>",
